# NetraSetu -- repo-root configuration.
#
# Each service now has its OWN .env.example next to its package.json, listing
# every variable it reads. Copy those (scripts/dev-up does it on first run):
#
#   central-system/backend/.env.example    central API, Postgres, MATLAB, auth, CORS
#   phc-local-app/backend/.env.example     PHC local API, CENTRAL_API_URL, PHC_CODE/ID/API_KEY
#   central-system/frontend/.env.example   VITE_CENTRAL_API_BASE, VITE_DATA_MODE
#   phc-local-app/frontend/.env.example    VITE_LOCAL_API_BASE, VITE_DATA_MODE
#   phc-local-app/mobile/.env.example      EXPO_PUBLIC_CENTRAL_API_URL, EXPO_PUBLIC_PHC_*
#   experimenting Frontend/.env.example    VITE_OPHTHALMOLOGIST_URL, VITE_NURSE_URL
#
# A <repo root>/.env is still read by both backends as a fallback after their
# own .env, so an existing shared file keeps working; a service's own .env wins.
#
# The only variables that belong HERE are the ones docker-compose.dev.yml reads
# (Compose loads the root .env for ${...} substitution). All optional.

# Host port the dev Postgres container is published on. 5433 so it never
# collides with a Postgres already installed on 5432. If you change it, change
# DATABASE_URL in central-system/backend/.env to match.
# NETRASETU_PG_PORT=5433
# NETRASETU_PG_PASSWORD=netrasetu_dev
